(4297554, 619450, 87469, '<td valign="top">I really like the this portrait, I would just take down the eyes a bit to match the body because even though you want to make the eyes pop out in the a portrait, you shouldn''t have them be over powering. <br/> <br/>To make the eyes really pop out, try putting a catch light in the shot. Not only does it save you time with photoshopping, but it also is the most capturing thing you can do in a portrait.<br/> <br/>Either way, I love everything else in the photograph. Just fix the eyes.</td>', 'I really like the this portrait, I would just take down the eyes a bit to match the body because even though you want to make the eyes pop out in the a portrait, you shouldn''t have them be over powering.  To make the eyes really pop out, try putting a catch light in the shot. Not only does it save you time with photoshopping, but it also is the most capturing thing you can do in a portrait. Either way, I love everything else in the photograph. Just fix the eyes.', '2007-12-06 22:26:38.000000', NULL, 1),
