(4305336, 618341, 67257, '<td valign="top">I think you did many things right with this picture.  The lighting and the background color both work well to emphases your hair.</td>', 'I think you did many things right with this picture.  The lighting and the background color both work well to emphases your hair.', '2007-12-10 04:51:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(4305372, 619827, 67257, '<td valign="top">Uhm I am torn over this picture.<br/> <br/>While I think this picture fits its title well, being homogeneous and free from dark shadows, I think a different technique would have made this image really pop.  A technique that would emphasize the texture and depth your hair and veil bring to this picture.  <br/> <br/>Something else I like about your submission is the fact that, while you captured your entire face, you do not show your eyes.  A majority of the picture in this challenge have added color processing to their eyes to help grab attention.  I like the fact that not only did you avoid that technique but you avoided showing your eyes all together.  It almost adds a level of suspense to the image.  Wanting or wondering what your eyes look like.  <br/> <br/>Overall great picture.  Good luck in the scoring.</td>', 'Uhm I am torn over this picture. While I think this picture fits its title well, being homogeneous and free from dark shadows, I think a different technique would have made this image really pop.  A technique that would emphasize the texture and depth your hair and veil bring to this picture.   Something else I like about your submission is the fact that, while you captured your entire face, you do not show your eyes.  A majority of the picture in this challenge have added color processing to their eyes to help grab attention.  I like the fact that not only did you avoid that technique but you avoided showing your eyes all together.  It almost adds a level of suspense to the image.  Wanting or wondering what your eyes look like.   Overall great picture.  Good luck in the scoring.', '2007-12-10 05:12:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(4305393, 619785, 67257, '<td valign="top">Overall picture is great.  I like the lighting and the use of black and white.  If I were scoring the images on beauty, you would be on top.  I think there are a few other pictures however that show some great creativity in their choice of surroundings.  <br/> <br/>Take this as a complement You look to young to know who Blondie is.  <br/> <br/>Good luck in the scoring.</td>', 'Overall picture is great.  I like the lighting and the use of black and white.  If I were scoring the images on beauty, you would be on top.  I think there are a few other pictures however that show some great creativity in their choice of surroundings.   Take this as a complement You look to young to know who Blondie is.   Good luck in the scoring.', '2007-12-10 05:22:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(4305414, 618741, 49578, '<td valign="top">i love the expression and the desat, but not sure abt the crop and the DoF</td>', 'i love the expression and the desat, but not sure abt the crop and the DoF', '2007-12-10 05:35:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(4305417, 617701, 67257, '<td valign="top">I think your image portrays the title well (it tells a story), I like the depth of field, and the use of the window to show your reflection.  Some simple things I would change to make this picture pop would be the lighting, levels and contrast.  <br/> <br/>With the lighting I would add some lighting behind you.  That would add an interesting effect with the wall behind you lighting up but without any shadows of you on it.  I don''t know what that would do to your reflection however.  Might have to experiment with that.<br/> <br/>I would adjust the levels and contracts to make the whites white.  The baseboard just doesnt appear to be a true color.  <br/> <br/>Overall I think it is a great picture.  Good luck in the scoring.</td>', 'I think your image portrays the title well (it tells a story), I like the depth of field, and the use of the window to show your reflection.  Some simple things I would change to make this picture pop would be the lighting, levels and contrast.   With the lighting I would add some lighting behind you.  That would add an interesting effect with the wall behind you lighting up but without any shadows of you on it.  I don''t know what that would do to your reflection however.  Might have to experiment with that. I would adjust the levels and contracts to make the whites white.  The baseboard just doesnt appear to be a true color.   Overall I think it is a great picture.  Good luck in the scoring.', '2007-12-10 05:35:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(4305419, 619128, 49578, '<td valign="top">Don''t quite get the title! Nice capture, though</td>', 'Don''t quite get the title! Nice capture, though', '2007-12-10 05:36:23.000000', NULL, 1),
