(4310837, 619850, 74273, '<td valign="top">Thank you for all the nice comments. I definitely agree that it is ever so slightly blurry. I liked the light too. It sort of seemed Vermeer-esque, in a way.</td>', 'Thank you for all the nice comments. I definitely agree that it is ever so slightly blurry. I liked the light too. It sort of seemed Vermeer-esque, in a way.', '2007-12-12 11:51:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4310840, 619619, 40973, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JuliBoc:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats on the Posthumous blue ribbon. Oh, and nice knees too. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sand has a magical way of clinging to everything.</td>', 'Originally posted by JuliBoc: Congrats on the Posthumous blue ribbon. Oh, and nice knees too.   Sand has a magical way of clinging to everything.', '2007-12-12 11:52:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4310857, 619910, 48471, '<td valign="top">Why is Peace the sexy thing, what happened to Justice? No more Wise Men to tell the Right from Wrong? I know there are a few out there...<br/> <br/>As for the photo, just like a few others, couldn''t tell that''s Iraq. Also, the V of fingers (wasn''t this what Sir Winston did to say that he won those Germans?), so the V of fingers doesn''t look very natural. Given the open but not smiling mouth, it rather looks like the globe, with everything in it, is falling and you are in great trouble to keep it there. Well, in a way, that''s the truth, isn''t it?<br/> <br/>The best thing in the photo is the hair: good light, good shapes and fluidity in it. In my opinion.</td>', 'Why is Peace the sexy thing, what happened to Justice? No more Wise Men to tell the Right from Wrong? I know there are a few out there... As for the photo, just like a few others, couldn''t tell that''s Iraq. Also, the V of fingers (wasn''t this what Sir Winston did to say that he won those Germans?), so the V of fingers doesn''t look very natural. Given the open but not smiling mouth, it rather looks like the globe, with everything in it, is falling and you are in great trouble to keep it there. Well, in a way, that''s the truth, isn''t it? The best thing in the photo is the hair: good light, good shapes and fluidity in it. In my opinion.', '2007-12-12 12:03:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4310885, 619709, 73981, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by briantammy:</b></div><hr/><i> underrated to me.  I think it should be 20-25 places higher.   wonderful and creative. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks...I was hoping for at least a top 10 actually...that is until I saw the others.</td>', 'Originally posted by briantammy: underrated to me.  I think it should be 20-25 places higher.   wonderful and creative.  Thanks...I was hoping for at least a top 10 actually...that is until I saw the others.', '2007-12-12 12:09:15.000000', NULL, 0),
