(4312377, 619288, 47483, '<td valign="top">So you again want an honest opinion. I can only speak for myself. I did not give it high score, I only gave it so so score. <br/>The only thing that put me off was its plasticky look. It was good compositions and something different. But the noise filter made it very unnatural for me. Felt as if it is not skin but a rubber stretched over the face. I am not sure how it would look without noise filter but it sure won''t be plasticky. This is what I felt. <br/>Sorry if it is too brutely honest but since you put an effort into it, you  should know what went wrong.</td>', 'So you again want an honest opinion. I can only speak for myself. I did not give it high score, I only gave it so so score. The only thing that put me off was its plasticky look. It was good compositions and something different. But the noise filter made it very unnatural for me. Felt as if it is not skin but a rubber stretched over the face. I am not sure how it would look without noise filter but it sure won''t be plasticky. This is what I felt. Sorry if it is too brutely honest but since you put an effort into it, you  should know what went wrong.', '2007-12-13 06:47:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4312451, 619288, 70375, '<td valign="top">I actually like this quite a bit. If I could change one thing, it would be to see more of your shoulder in the right image of you. Very minor detail as I can''t stop looking at your eyes anyway. It is perhaps the monitor problem that caused some of the low votes. Of course, I like the "edited" face look. I did some very light editing on mine and still got the "you over edited this" comments. LOL You should be proud to be able to add this to your portfolio. It is very creative and very unusual and your lighting is excellent. As Monica mentioned, the differences in expression are also very captivating and interesting :)<br/> <br/>Gosh, sorry that is so long, but I hope it helps :) Also, your average vote from commenters is really really good :)</td>', 'I actually like this quite a bit. If I could change one thing, it would be to see more of your shoulder in the right image of you. Very minor detail as I can''t stop looking at your eyes anyway. It is perhaps the monitor problem that caused some of the low votes. Of course, I like the "edited" face look. I did some very light editing on mine and still got the "you over edited this" comments. LOL You should be proud to be able to add this to your portfolio. It is very creative and very unusual and your lighting is excellent. As Monica mentioned, the differences in expression are also very captivating and interesting :) Gosh, sorry that is so long, but I hope it helps :) Also, your average vote from commenters is really really good :)', '2007-12-13 08:02:58.000000', NULL, 0),
