(4316339, 619411, 87785, '<td valign="top">the angle is just fantastic !</td>', 'the angle is just fantastic !', '2007-12-15 18:49:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4316447, 617960, 37105, '<td valign="top">This really is a fascinating self-portrait. To me, this is what this contest was all about. "Chapeau!" as we say in french...!!</td>', 'This really is a fascinating self-portrait. To me, this is what this contest was all about. "Chapeau!" as we say in french...!!', '2007-12-15 21:30:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4316453, 619922, 37105, '<td valign="top">Absolutely fascinating. This is what I like about a (self-)portrait: an image that let you want to know more! Congrat for this one, way underscored is you ask me...</td>', 'Absolutely fascinating. This is what I like about a (self-)portrait: an image that let you want to know more! Congrat for this one, way underscored is you ask me...', '2007-12-15 21:42:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4316474, 619731, 25618, '<td valign="top">very good work Gett....getting better all the time</td>', 'very good work Gett....getting better all the time', '2007-12-15 22:16:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4316543, 619411, 63503, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Debbi:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice use of Lucis too<br/>Debbi </i></td></tr></table> <br/>No Lucis or other plugins here, Rene explained that he under-exposed by 2 stops (measuring on the sky) and used 2 lights (probably monolights) to lit himself, one from the front (and probably below) and and the second one from behind (to his right). Intended or not, it is apparent that the latter provided additional lighting to his left side by reflecting in the sliding glass door. He then dodged/burnt and partially desaturated the red channel, that''s it. The result is obviously stunning. The message is the one we all know but tend to forget so often: proper lighting and exposure is what really counts.</td>', 'Originally posted by Debbi: Nice use of Lucis tooDebbi  No Lucis or other plugins here, Rene explained that he under-exposed by 2 stops (measuring on the sky) and used 2 lights (probably monolights) to lit himself, one from the front (and probably below) and and the second one from behind (to his right). Intended or not, it is apparent that the latter provided additional lighting to his left side by reflecting in the sliding glass door. He then dodged/burnt and partially desaturated the red channel, that''s it. The result is obviously stunning. The message is the one we all know but tend to forget so often: proper lighting and exposure is what really counts.', '2007-12-15 23:13:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4317285, 619956, 87502, '<td valign="top">This SP is absolutely breathtaking!  Your camera sees deep.</td>', 'This SP is absolutely breathtaking!  Your camera sees deep.', '2007-12-16 16:00:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4317524, 619785, 68516, '<td valign="top">Beautiful...the picture and yourself :)</td>', 'Beautiful...the picture and yourself :)', '2007-12-16 21:03:58.000000', NULL, 0),
